set.body:
Build a fitted projection facade over OperatorBlockPartition, block-local FunctionalFrames, fitted block preprocessors, and explicit combination weights.

Expose global projection, unweighted projectBlock scores, weighted blockContribution scores, and arbitrary identity-bound partial projection. Keep the existing direct-sum and partially aligned MultisetAssociation core unchanged.

Acceptance:
- the sum of block contributions equals global projection;
- projectBlock and blockContribution are observably distinct;
- global and block-local feature identities cannot be mixed;
- arbitrary partial projection delegates to the same FeatureRestriction machinery as single-table fits;
- blockwise preprocessors are reused without refitting;
- full, block, partial, sparse, and foreign-structure laws pass on JVM and Scala.js.
